    <string name="app_name">XQZ Enabler</string>
    <string name="app_title">XQZ Monitor Enabler</string>
    <string name="start">Start</string>
    <string name="stop">Stop</string>

    <string name="help_text">1. Turn the monitor screen switch ON and connect it to the phone.\n\n2. On Samsung phones, turn OFF DeX auto-start:\nSettings &gt; Connected devices &gt; Samsung DeX &gt;\n&quot;Auto start when HDMI is connected&quot; = off.\n\n3. Tap Start and allow USB access. Choose &quot;Always open XQZ Enabler&quot; so a replug reconnects without another tap.\n\n4. Open the Camera app. The phone OS mirrors the screen to the monitor.\n\nIf DeX starts instead, switch to Screen mirroring from the notification, or turn off DeX auto-start and reconnect. The Xperia mirrors directly.\n\nKeep the notification enabled for the Stop action; the Quick Settings tile starts and stops the service while it is running, and retries or opens this app while waiting. Without the &quot;Always open&quot; choice, Android asks for USB access again after a replug.</string>

    <string name="footer">\nIf the camera preview is black on the monitor, the camera app is probably blocking screen capture; that is the signal to try the MediaProjection path.</string>

